    "partNumber": 4,
    "transcript": "Test 1 Part 4. Impact of cars in Australia 1940s-1990s. public transport 60% (31); buses crowded and uncomfortable (32); cars associated with freedom (33); new government 1949 (35); high taxes on cars (34); streets congested and polluted (36); roads had more lanes (37); affected relationships (38); new advertisements (39); shopping malls (40).",
    "formContent": "<div class=\"ielts-form-container\"><div class=\"form-section\"><div class=\"form-title\" style=\"text-align:center;font-weight:700;\">Impact of cars in Australia (1940s - 1990s)</div><p><strong>1940s</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>One person in eight owned a car</li><li><input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"31\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"> transport was used for 60% of journeys</li><li>Buses:</li></ul><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">Problems &ndash; crowded and <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"32\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"></p><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">Advantage &ndash; affordable</p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>Cars were associated with <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"33\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"></li><li>Problems of car ownerships</li></ul><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">i. cost</p><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">ii. many spare parts were imported</p><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">iii. Result of pressure from motorists - new <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"35\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"> in Australia in 1949</p><p><strong>1960s</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>Cars were cheaper and more reliable</li></ul><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">More people restrictions on fuel</p><p style=\"margin-left:20px;\">iv. high <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"34\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"> on cars</p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>lived in the suburbs</li><li>Main streets were congested and <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"36\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"> (and usually straight)</li><li>New streets were built with curves to make drivers slow down</li></ul><p><strong>1970s</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>Roads had more <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"37\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"></li><li>More commuters</li><li>Car use affected the <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"38\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"> between people</li><li>New types of <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"39\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"> were designed to attract motorists</li></ul><p><strong>1980s and 1990s</strong></p><ul style=\"line-height:2;\"><li>Less business in town centres because of introduction of <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"40\" style=\"width:140px;text-align:center;\"></li><li>Introduction of drive-in facilities, e.g. restaurants</li></ul></div></div>",
